4. Limitations

You may use the Software only for a Permitted Purpose. A "Permitted Purpose" is
any purpose other than a Commercial Purpose.

5. Commercial Purposes

"Commercial Purpose" means the purpose of monetary reward or commercial
advantage, including:

  a. selling, leasing, licensing, sublicensing, or otherwise exchanging the
     Software for money or anything else of value;

  b. providing a product or service that uses the Software for which you charge
     a fee, collect subscription revenue, or otherwise receive compensation;

  c. using the Software within a business process, service, or product that is
     operated for profit or supports revenue-generating activity;

  d. offering paid support, consulting, integration, or customization services
     based on the Software.

6. Notices

You must ensure that everyone who gets a copy of any part of the Software from
You, with or without changes, also gets the text of this License or a link to
<https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0>.

7. Excuse

If anyone notifies You in writing that You have not complied with Notices, You
can keep Your licenses by taking all practical steps to comply within 30 days
after the notice. If You do not do so, Your licenses end immediately.

8. Patent License

The licensor grants You a patent license for any patent claims the licensor can
license, or becomes able to license, that You would infringe by using the
Software for any Permitted Purpose.

9. Noncommercial Organizations

If You are a noncommercial organization, such as a school, charity, or
government body, and use the Software solely for a Permitted Purpose, that use
is allowed under this License.

10. No Other Rights

These licenses do not allow You to sublicense or transfer any of Your licenses
